xnu 0475: start the wifi worker after every probe, and premap the pins

Measured 2026-11-26: each boot stops at a different `ml_io_map()` inside the
wifi worker -- `W4 BAR map done` (0469), `pcie0 link up` (0470), `pcie0 gdsc up`
(0473, `wifi_map_host`), and `early GCC 0x62008` (0474, `wifi_map_pins`). The
window moves with the premap, so the window is not the fault: the worker runs
while the boot probe block still maps its own windows (audio, Venus, BT all
follow `mondrian_usb_probe()`, which started the worker), and `ml_io_map()` is
serialized.

Two changes. The seven TLMM pin pages join the premap, so the worker's cold
link has no mapping left at all. And `mondrian_wifi_start()` moves out of
`mondrian_usb_probe()` to the end of the boot probe block, so no other probe is
still mapping when the worker begins.
diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
index 97bebd9..c56f199 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
@@ -2402,6 +2402,7 @@ mondrian_log_start(void)
 		extern void mondrian_spmi_probe(void);
 		extern void mondrian_reset_reason_init(void);
 		extern void mondrian_wifi_premap(void);
+		extern void mondrian_wifi_start(void);
 
 		/*
 		 * Both map MMIO and must run before any worker that maps: the
@@ -2420,6 +2421,13 @@ mondrian_log_start(void)
 		mondrian_venus_start();
 		mondrian_bt_tty_init();
 		mondrian_bt_ctl_init();
+		/*
+		 * Last, so the worker starts after every other probe has taken
+		 * its mappings: an ml_io_map() in the worker racing one of them
+		 * blocks for good (measured 2026-11-26, four boots stopped at a
+		 * different worker window each time).
+		 */
+		mondrian_wifi_start();
 	}
 }
 
